# Olo: the computer's human presence sensor (a ThinkPad's, in its camera
# module: the HID sensor hub's "prox"), read by the session to lock the
# screen when the person walks away and wake it when they come back
# (Preferences ▸ Power ▸ Presence). Its buffer carries a sample as
# presence or attention changes, once a second at most; reading `_raw`
# would ask the sensor each time. Installed by Olo Doctor and
# tools/install-session.sh.
ACTION=="add|change", SUBSYSTEM=="iio", ATTR{name}=="prox", TAG+="uaccess", ATTR{in_proximity0_sampling_frequency}="1", ATTR{scan_elements/in_proximity0_en}="1", ATTR{scan_elements/in_attention_en}="1", ATTR{buffer/enable}="1"
